    /* THE SHIP (2026-10-28, mondo: "i dont like the spaceship map. it just looks like a big slab slapped on top of a spaceship. can we
       redo it and make it better. why not give the spaceship wings and have the spawn zones be in each wing ... The maps dont have to be
       square. There can be gaps and pathways etc. Really try to make a good realistic spaceship map"): THE DECK is no longer a plate on
       a fuselage — it IS THE SHIP, drawn square by square on the battle squares (hqDeckPlan, the plan below: one string per lattice row,
       north first; the lattice is 36 × 28 squares, x = −31.5 + 1.75 col, z = −24.5 + 1.75 row) over THE VOID (terrain.void — the room's
       own floor is open space, the Astral sea's rule: no ground, a fall comes back to the last ground stood on, the field reads it as
       open sky). Bow east, stern west: THE HULL down the middle (four squares wide, the nose tapering to two), THE WINGS swept back off
       it either side (the port wing north, the starboard wing south — the two teams' spawns in every arena cut), THE ENGINE PODS astern
       outboard of the stern on their pylons and spars, THE CANARDS forward, THE BRIDGE one level up on the nose and THE ENGINE HOUSING
       one level up on the stern (a steel flight up each), a crate block each side of the nexus and one on each wing, A BREACH blown
       through each wing root, and the docking boom out of each wingtip to the rim: the AIRLOCK's collar on the port boom (deck level —
       the airlock's floor), the bay door on the starboard boom. THE STARSHIP under it (three-renderer.js _hqBuildStarship — float.hull
       kind 'starship'): the plan's own silhouette as the ship's sides, its belly, the round keel under the hull, the engine bells and
       the pods' nacelles astern, the lit edge strips, the bridge's windows, the running lights. THE VOYAGE as before. Every arena size is
       cut across the wings and the hull (HQ_ARENA_RULES.within.prebuilt_derelict). */
    /* THE GUNSHIP (2026-11-11, mondo: "redesign the spaceship. It just looks nothing like a spaceship at all. Surely you can make it look
       like a legitimate spaceship while also keeping the square grid in mind and designing the map for interesting and strategic PVP
       play" · "why not put the spawn zones at either end of the ship. I feel like putting it the way it is now kinda defeats the purpose
       and just makes the map 1 dimensional"): the 10-28 ship (wings 120 m wide, the board a small window on its flat middle) is
       redrawn as a COMPACT GUNSHIP LENGTHWISE on the board — bow NORTH, stern SOUTH, the teams spawning at either end of the ship.
       The lattice is 34 × 28 squares of 3.5 m (x = −59.5 + 3.5 col, z = −49 + 3.5 row); the 12 × 12 board is cols 11..22, rows 8..19
       (x −21..21, z −21..21), mirrored port / starboard AND bow / stern so both teams get the same board: THE SPINE (the dorsal deck,
       six squares wide) bow to stern with a spawn deck at each end and the nexus hatch amidships; beside each spawn THE SPONSONS
       (bow) / THE ENGINE HOUSINGS (stern) one level up, each joined to its wing by THE PYLON (a one-square catwalk over the void);
       THE WING ROOTS amidships with THE WING GUNS (a 2 × 2 casemate two levels up, its step one level, the contested high ground the
       same distance from both spawns); an escape pod by each spawn's corner and a sensor dish at each corner of the hatch (one-square
       ghost blocks). Three lanes: the spine (open: the house tiles), and a flank each side (sponson → pylon → the gun → pylon →
       housing), joined across the wing roots. Off the board: THE BRIDGE (one level up, the canopy on its face) and the nose with the
       airlock's collar (north wall, x 0); THE ENGINE BLOCK (the reactor stack two levels up) with the five bells on its aft face; THE
       WINGS swept back from the roots, a nacelle under each tip (`pods`), the docked fighters, the docking arm off the starboard wing to
       the bay door (south wall). THE STARSHIP draws the hull with the bow north (`bow: 'n'`: the parts in the keel's frame, `along` −z).
       Every arena size is cut round the hatch (HQ_ARENA_RULES.within.prebuilt_derelict). */
    /* THE CRUISER (2026-11-11, mondo on the gunship: "it still just looks like a floating rectangle" · "the battlefield and the map do
       not have to be flat ... A ship is generally more clyndrical. I expect there to be ramps and stairs on a ship ... shape it like
       an actual spaceship, you are not confined to making it a rectangle" · "make sure i am able to walk on those boosters, thats what
       i mean by verticality. I shouldnt be confined to just the top of the ship that is all straight and flat. Those boosters are
       lower, and i want to walk on the side/edge of the ship where it is lower" · "and the wings" · the docking arm: "that one part
       sticking off the side is kind of useless"): the ship is a ROUND HULL and the decks are cut on it at three levels. Same lattice
       and board (cols 11..22, rows 8..19), bow north, the teams at the bow and the stern; the plan's 'o' is now THE LOWER LEVEL (3.2 m).
       · THE FLIGHT DECK ('1', 6.7 m): the hull's crown, four squares wide (board cols 4..7), bow to stern — both spawn decks, the nexus
         hatch. HQ_ARENA_RULES.houseTile stands this site's house one level over its lowest ground.
       · THE SIDE WALKWAYS ('o', cols 3 and 8): a level down on the hull's shoulders, the whole length, round the nose to the airlock.
       · THE PODS ('o', cols 0..1 / 10..11, rows 0..2 and 9..11): the two BOOSTERS aft and the two GUN PODS forward, a square of open
         space between each and the hull (`proud` 0.45: a one-square void reads as void).
       · THE WINGS ('o', cols 0..2 / 9..11, rows 4..7, swept on three squares past the board): THE TURRET two levels up on each
         (cols 0 / 11, rows 5..6 — the sniper's perch, five squares off the hatch), its step one level up inboard of it.
       · THE STAIRS: four ramps (rows 3 and 8, each side) from the strut between pod and wing up onto the flight deck — 8.4 m of run
         (from 1.4 m inside the foot square to the deck's edge: the walker's 1.46 m step between square middles).
       · Off the board: the bridge (two up, the canopy before it) and the nose deck at the airlock's level; the engine block aft; the
         outer wings with the fighters. The docking arm is gone: the bay door stands free on the nose deck (siteRooms.backDoors).
       THE HULL: three-renderer.js _hqShipParts (float.hull.tube / nacelles / wings / cannons / canopies / masts). */
