/* THE WHOLE MODEL LIST IN THE EDITOR (2026-11-09, mondo: "Everything in the model list should be available in the map editor"): every
   model file on R2 (MODEL_LIST.md, R2_MODEL_FILES.json) that no catalogue row named yet, so the editor's MODELS tab can place it. Made
   once by a scratch script (the thread "Make every model list asset placeable in editor"): the files' own bounds read from their glTF
   headers. The packs (PSX Mega Pack, Elbolilloduro, Halloween) are real metres, so `h` / `span` IS the file's size; the Meshy files are
   unit-sized, so they carry a size picked by hand per thing. `group` = the palette group, `base: 'asset'` = `file` is the bucket path
   under Assets/ (data.js hqCatalogueFilePath, three-renderer.js _hqModelUrl). No row is placed in any room; none changes a rule. Left
   out on purpose: the meshy_decor files a proc row already wears (placeable under the proc's key), the traps' "-colonly" collision
   shells, the stairs kit sheets (the BUILD stairs tools cut them), FBX / DAE / .blend / OBJ copies of a GLB that is in, eagle.glb (the
   raw upload no loader reads; eagle_rigged is the animal), the creator's clothes / hair / bodies and the animation libraries (they
   dress a body; the races and the cast are the PEOPLE tab). The OBJ trees the TREES tab lacked are HQ_TREE_KINDS tree_21+. */
